e":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration_policy.md#7D65]\n1:# Migration Policy\n2:\n3:The migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n4:\n5:Dirty email cleanup rules:\n6:- Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n7:- The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n8:- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n9:- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n10:- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n11:\n12:Schema rules:\n13:- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n14:- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n15:- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n16:- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n17:\n18:Rollback:\n19:- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n20:- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n21:- It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users."}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788191452081},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3A0ldk4o04NKNJo5ak9LCm5M|fc_0ba7eea486d8d8f1016a95a2dbe9c087d291769b35b73e7d39","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/schema.sql#14EF]\n1:PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n2:\n3:CREATE TABLE users (\n4:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:    email TEXT,\n6:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n8:);\n9:\n10:INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n11:('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n12:('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n13:('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n14:('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n15:('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n16:('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n17:\n18:CREATE TABLE orders (\n19:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n20:    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n21:    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n22:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n23:);\n24:\n25:INSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at) VALUES\n26:('o1', 'u1', 1299, '2024-04-01T09:00:00Z'),\n27:('o2', 'u4', 4599, '2024-04-02T10:30:00Z'),\n28:('o3', 'u5', 799, '2024-04-03T11:45:00Z'),\n29:('o4', 'u6', 1599, '2024-04-04T12:10:00Z');"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788191452081},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_F6vlXNqmHxcuo7XX5dikJVZ1|fc_0ba7eea486d8d8f1016a95a2dbe9cc87d29a51afc3e5541119","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration.sql#C701]\n1:DROP TABLE users;\n2:\n3:CREATE TABLE users (\n4:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n6:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n8:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n9:);"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788191452081},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning idempotent SQLite migration**\n\n**Designing backup and schema check for migration**\n\n**Planning idempotent migration with marker table**\n\n**Designing idempotent user migration**\n\n**Planning status preservation and email constraints**\n\n**Verifying conditional column addition support**\n\n**Verifying SQLite ALTER TABLE capabilities**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ba7eea486d8d8f1016a95a2dd109487d28239142bba1639e0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning idempotent SQLite migration**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text